WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.260
Falcon Heavy Side Boosters separated at 2 minutes 27 seconds on NRL 97. This is SpaceX Daily, episode

00:00:08.260 --> 00:00:16.640
119. The side boosters separated about 2 minutes 27 seconds after liftoff on the NRL 97 mission.

00:00:17.240 --> 00:00:23.700
The launch lifted off from launch complex 39A at Kennedy Space Center, Florida, at 11.54

00:00:23.700 --> 00:00:31.320
PM Eastern time on October 1st, 2026. Both boosters returned to Cape Canaveral and landed at landing

00:00:31.320 --> 00:00:37.520
zones 1 and 2. It was Falcon Heavy's 14th flight and its first mission for the National Reconnaissance

00:00:37.520 --> 00:00:45.380
Office. Video of the separation came from SpaceX. SpaceX listed the SDA's 4th Tronch 1 mission on

00:00:45.380 --> 00:00:51.480
its launches page. The entry appears under the company's active launch manifest. SpaceX shared

00:00:51.480 --> 00:00:55.560
this downward-facing view of hot staging on Starship Flight 14.

00:00:56.300 --> 00:01:02.380
Ship 41's Raptor engines ignited during stage separation as Super Heavy Booster 21 separated

00:01:02.380 --> 00:01:03.080
beneath it.

00:01:03.700 --> 00:01:08.440
The flight reached orbit from Starbase Texas on September 28th, 2026.

00:01:09.240 --> 00:01:13.660
The view captures the moment the upper-stage engine started while the booster fell away.

00:01:14.160 --> 00:01:19.600
The Falcon 9 booster houses 9 Merlins while the second stage uses a single Merlin vacuum

00:01:19.600 --> 00:01:20.060
engine.

00:01:20.060 --> 00:01:26.620
A sea-level Merlin produces about 190,000 pounds of thrust, and the vacuum version reaches

00:01:26.620 --> 00:01:29.300
up to 220,500 pounds.

00:01:29.900 --> 00:01:36.040
The Raptor uses full-flow staged combustion and produces 617,000 pounds of thrust per

00:01:36.040 --> 00:01:36.380
engine.

00:01:37.100 --> 00:01:41.660
Starship carries 33 Raptors on the super-heavy booster and 6 on the ship.

00:01:42.520 --> 00:01:47.860
Merlin engines run on rocket-grade kerosene and liquid oxygen, while Raptors burn liquid

00:01:47.860 --> 00:01:49.000
methane and oxygen.

00:01:49.000 --> 00:01:54.960
The crew supported research that benefits life on Earth and prepares humans for deep space missions.

00:01:55.740 --> 00:01:58.580
NASA astronauts Jessica Muir and Jack Hathaway,

00:01:59.160 --> 00:02:01.300
ESA astronaut Sophie Adinot,

00:02:01.820 --> 00:02:04.940
and Ross Cosmos Cosmonaut Andre Fedyev,

00:02:05.120 --> 00:02:06.860
will return in early October.

00:02:07.560 --> 00:02:12.000
Research and microgravity covered changes in cell behavior and material formation.

00:02:12.680 --> 00:02:17.480
The FAA launched a supplemental environmental assessment on SpaceX's proposal

00:02:17.480 --> 00:02:24.780
for SLC37 at Cape Canaveral. The proposal covers up to 76 starship super heavy launches

00:02:24.780 --> 00:02:31.580
and 152 landings per year. The review studies environmental and airspace effects before

00:02:31.580 --> 00:02:38.000
any license modification. Commercial operations at the pad remain on hold until the process concludes.

00:02:38.800 --> 00:02:44.620
The 50-foot bronze Prometheus statue near Starbase reached completion. The finished sculpture

00:02:44.620 --> 00:02:51.460
stands outside the Texas launch site. Elon Musk stated SpaceX holds rank 1 while Grock leads

00:02:51.460 --> 00:02:58.480
GPT-6 in cyber defense benchmarks. The claim ties SpaceX performance to XAI model results.

00:02:59.280 --> 00:03:04.240
Observers on the SpaceX subreddit noted the steeper ascent profile on flight 14.

00:03:04.880 --> 00:03:11.320
The change appears tied to orbital insertion preparations. The refrigerator sized MVP satellite

00:03:11.320 --> 00:03:17.860
carries four-tensor processing units. It flew as a ride share on Transportor 18 from Vandenberg

00:03:17.860 --> 00:03:24.800
on October 1st, 2026. The payload tests whether the chip survived launch vibration and space

00:03:24.800 --> 00:03:31.880
radiation under Project Suncatcher. Crew 13 arrived after a 7-hour 55-minute dragon flight.

00:03:32.500 --> 00:03:41.300
The station now hosts 11 people. The new crew includes NASA astronauts Jessica Watkins and Luke

00:03:41.300 --> 00:03:46.620
astronaut Joshua Kutrick and Ross Cosmos Cosmonaut Sergei Teteriatnikov.

00:03:46.920 --> 00:03:53.100
The crew 13 launch occurred from Florida aboard a Falcon 9, drag and docked at the International

00:03:53.100 --> 00:03:55.720
Space Station after the record-setting flight.

00:03:56.480 --> 00:04:02.420
One thing worth watching is the FAA Supplemental Environmental Assessment for up to 76 starship

00:04:02.420 --> 00:04:05.760
super-heavy launches per year at SLC 37.

00:04:05.760 --> 00:04:11.460
A Google representative called the payload of very minimal test rather than a full orbital

00:04:11.460 --> 00:04:12.820
data center demonstration.

00:04:13.380 --> 00:04:18.040
The four TPUs provide roughly the compute of a single data center server.

00:04:18.600 --> 00:04:23.900
From an engineering standpoint, the shift from gas generator Merlin engines to full flow

00:04:23.900 --> 00:04:28.400
staged combustion raptors changes how propellant energy converts to thrust.

00:04:29.260 --> 00:04:34.240
In a gas generator cycle, a separate turbine burns a small propellant stream to drive

00:04:34.240 --> 00:04:40.800
the pumps, discarding that exhaust and limiting overall efficiency. Full flow staged combustion

00:04:40.800 --> 00:04:46.420
routes all propellant through the turbines first, extracting more work before the main chamber burns

00:04:46.420 --> 00:04:52.000
it, which raises specific impulse and allows higher chamber pressures without extra hardware mass.

00:04:52.820 --> 00:04:59.480
The Raptors 617,000 pounds of thrust per engine, versus the Merlin's 190,000 pounds,

00:04:59.480 --> 00:05:04.740
reflects that thermodynamic gain plus the switch to denser methane-oxygen propellant.

00:05:05.560 --> 00:05:10.520
Manufacturing the more complex Raptor cycle requires tighter tolerances on turbo pump

00:05:10.520 --> 00:05:12.080
seals and injector elements.

00:05:12.700 --> 00:05:17.700
Yet the payoff appears in Starship's ability to carry 33 engines on a single booster,

00:05:18.120 --> 00:05:19.880
while still targeting rapid reuse.

00:05:20.660 --> 00:05:25.680
The same cycle also reduces the number of engine variants needed across sea level and vacuum

00:05:25.680 --> 00:05:28.960
versions, because the core architecture stays consistent.

00:05:29.620 --> 00:05:34.980
Raw material costs for a single Raptor sit far below the finished engine price, creating

00:05:34.980 --> 00:05:39.840
an idiot index that SpaceX aims to compress through iteration and volume production.

